    "description": "Worked on developing autonomous mobile robots.\n• Developed a brake plugin using C++ to enable the robotic platform to spawn on an uneven surface in \n  the gazebo simulation, which also added the functionality of stopping the robotic motion during the \n  simulation.\n• Developed a contact plugin using C++ to know which part of the robot collides with objects in the \n  gazebo environment, to better understand the improvements needed in planning algorithms.\n• Developed various geofences included in YAML files to test whether a robot can perform a difficult task in \n   varying geographical features during the simulation.\n• Developed a custom gazebo world much like a real environment to improve the test cases using OpenGL \n   and Sketchup objects.\n• Extended the URDF/SDF robot descriptions to include the developed plugins.\n• Extended the nightly testing scripts to include new packages and perform regression testing.",
